],"note":"Closed Sun; Typical hours — check the official site"},"summary":"The King Fahad National Library is the legal deposit and copyright library for Saudi Arabia. The project was announced in 1983 in response to an initiative made by the people of Riyadh when King Fahd ascended the throne, and the implementation started in 1986. The library opened in Riyadh in 1990.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"King Fahad National Library","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9e/King_Fahad_Library.jpg","thumb":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9e/King_Fahad_Library.jpg","w":1200,"h":675,"author":"Ayesha46","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_Fahad_Library.jpg"}},{"id":"riyadh_salam_park","areaId":"riyadh","name":"Salam Park","category":"park","tags":["nature","photo"],"location":{"lat":24.62083,"lng":46.70833},"visitMinutes":60,"priceLevel":0,"photoSeed":"riyadh_salam_park","tickets":[],"signals":{"commonsDepicts":2,"commonsNearby":2,"wikiPageviews":200,"wikidataSitelinks":2,"fetchedAt":"2026-10-18"},"hashtags":["salampark","riyadh"],"bestLight":"golden","summary":"Salam Park is a 61-acre historic urban park in the al-Salam district of Riyadh, Saudi Arabia, located southwest of Qasr al-Hukm District. Opened in 2004, it was built on the site of an eponymous date palm orchard that belonged to Prince Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman.","summarySource":"wikipedia","wikipediaTitle":"Salam Park","photo":{"url":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Families_Salam_Park_Riyadh.jpg/1280px-Families_Salam_Park_Riyadh.jpg","thumb":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a1/Families_Salam_Park_Riyadh.jpg/500px-Families_Salam_Park_Riyadh.jpg","w":1200,"h":1600,"author":"Hamza A. Durrani","license":"CC BY 4.0","licenseUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.or